  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nWith troughing over British Columbia and high pressure aloft \nover the Four Corners, hot, dry, and breezy conditions will \ncontinue to end the week. This pattern doesn't appear promising \nin reducing impacts from wildfire smoke. Smoke acting to block \nincoming solar radiation could be a failure mode in terms of the\ntemperature forecast. The general pattern would favor \ntemperatures climbing to around 5 degrees above normal Thursday \nthrough Saturday, as the high pressure aloft shifts to be over \nthe Great Basin... but smoke impacts may moderate temperatures \nto be near normal. Come Sunday, the aforementioned British \nColumbia trough and it's associated cold front will cross over \nour area. This will be a dry cold frontal passage, bringing \ngusty winds, and near or even slightly below normal temperatures\ncome Sunday and Monday.",
